            <ArticleTitle>Coronary arterial occlusion and myocardial infarction in acute myocarditis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>226-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary arterial occlusion may occur experimentally during acute myocarditis but has not been documented in man. We report the case of a young female with severe myocarditis who later required cardiac transplantation and in whom coronary occlusion was demonstrated arteriographically before transplantation and by pathological examination of the heart after explantation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
